    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d393">

                <pb facs="0369" n="362" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg362"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9125: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-09T16:00:00-04:00">August 9, 1937—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s July 31, 1 p.m.,<anchor n="74" xml:id="d393-f1"/> and your August 7,
                    10 a.m. Can you confirm press reports to the effect that Japanese military and
                    civilian residents at Hankow have now almost completely evacuated the Japanese
                    Concession; that the administration of the Japanese Concession has been turned
                    over temporarily to Chinese officials; and that the Communist army is moving out
                    of Shensi into Suiyuan?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
